+# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
+# Copyright (c) 2026 Jay Leaton. The DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash family of TensorFold (Apache-2.0): see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
+"""Log probabilities on the V4.1 server (``logprobs.py``): the whole vocabulary's log-softmax over four uneven
+
+slices, the OpenAI reply shape, the batcher's plumbing, and every request the server must refuse by name.
+
+- ``logprobs.parts`` / ``combine``: the ranks' (max, sum of exp) parts of the uneven 128-block split
+  (256 / 128 / 128 / 128 of 640 here; the real model's 32,384 / 32,384 / 32,256 / 32,256) combine to the same
+  log-sum-exp one rank's full row gives, and the mass over the whole vocabulary sums to 1 (the 5/5/4/4 block-split
+  bug class: a normalizer computed per slice would not);
+- the real forward on four CPU threads (``cand_gather`` with ``probs``): ``Candidates.lse`` matches one rank's
+  ``logsumexp``, every rank's is bit-identical, and without ``probs`` there is no normalizer (and no extra columns);
+- the batcher on the fake forward: an emitted token's log probability is its verify row's logit minus that
+  normalizer, ``top_logprobs`` is the row's top N in the merged candidates' order, a masked (-inf) column never
+  appears, and a request that did not ask is decoded token for token as before;
+- refusals: malformed ``logprobs`` / ``top_logprobs`` / ``n``, and the modes the server does not implement
+  (streaming, thinking on, tools, stop strings, structured output, ``logit_bias`` / ``prompt_logprobs`` / ``echo``).
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import numpy as np
+import pytest
+
+torch = pytest.importorskip("torch")
